{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ada Script is AdaEngine’s scripting layer for gameplay and ECS integration. Its source files use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ada"},{"type":"text","text":" extension. The current implementation uses an embedded language runtime, while the public API, diagnostics, and tooling consistently present Ada Script concepts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Annotations are not only syntax. AdaEngine resolves every query into native archetypes and component columns and publishes its component access to the scheduler."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use Ada Script for gameplay rules that benefit from quick iteration. Keep rendering backends, custom data structures, and other low-level or performance-critical facilities in Swift.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"ada","type":"codeListing","code":["@system(scheduler: \"update\")","class MovementSystem {","    @query(Transform, Movement)","    var movers;","","    func update(context) {","        for (var entity in movers) {","            var position = entity.transform.position;","            var velocity = entity.movement.velocity;","            position[0] += velocity[0] * context.deltaTime;","            position[1] += velocity[1] * context.deltaTime;","            entity.transform.position = position;","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"AdaEditor projects configure automatic script discovery by default. For an existing Swift package, follow ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/GettingStartedWithAdaScript","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to enable the build plugin and register the generated script plugins.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Ada Script","modules":[{"name":"Ada Script"}],"roleHea